# Cloudflare uploads everything not listed here as a public static asset,
# so without these the repo's own documentation would be served from the
# site: flield.com/README.md, /CONTRIBUTING.md, and the issue templates were
# all returning 200 and were indexable as thin duplicates of pages that
# already exist. They belong on GitHub; a 404 is the right answer here.
*.md
.github

# Repo config, likewise not part of the site.
.gitignore
.assetsignore
wrangler.jsonc

.git
.wrangler

# What .gitignore keeps out of the repo is still on disk in a working
# folder, and Wrangler does not read .gitignore. The site deploys from a
# clean clone, where none of this exists, so these lines change nothing
# there. They are for a `wrangler deploy` run by hand from a folder
# someone works in, which would otherwise publish local/ (analytics
# exports, plans, drafts) and an editor's settings as static assets.
# Keep this list in step with .gitignore.
local
.claude
__pycache__
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Tells GitHub Pages not to run Jekyll. It means nothing to Cloudflare,
# which was serving the empty file at /.nojekyll.
.nojekyll
